body:
Owner-requested audit found a plausible no-op assumption that may suppress an original action.

[ArmyTransferModel.ComposeOk](https://github.com/diegoami/imperial_conquest_2/blob/4d70275aac4e155c0370a3ee23525cf34450a908/godot/UI/Dialogs/ArmyDialogModels.cs#L381) returns null when no units/resources were staged. [ArmyTransferCommandHandler](https://github.com/diegoami/imperial_conquest_2/blob/4d70275aac4e155c0370a3ee23525cf34450a908/src/IC2.Engine/Armies/Commands/ArmyTransferCommandHandler.cs#L66) also rejects an all-zero order. Its test Transfer_WithNoUnitsSupplyOrMoney_IsRejectedAndTheStateIsUntouched explains that an empty order moves nothing, but tests only a balanced state. That premise is not established for an over-cap army.

The [promoted TArmyToArmy_OK report](https://github.com/diegoami/imperial-conquest-2-research/blob/865755e04f107afc38cdb496669d882e2551aca6/docs/reports/2026-10-03-army-to-army-ok-supply-rebalancing.md) reads unconditional writes and supply push: selected army A's excess over troops/100 goes to B, then B's excess goes back to A; nothing refuses OK. Existing T117/build636 implemented rebalancing after an accepted changed order. The report lacks live over-cap no-edit-OK confirmation.

Please trace initialization/dirty flags/OK callbacks, then compare minimal controls:
- A over-cap and B with room, open Transfer and press OK with no edits;
- identical input, Cancel;
- reverse selected army and repeat;
- both within capacity, and both over capacity;
- if covered by the same handler, unit disband inside the dialog followed by OK, keeping resource/move effects separately attributed.

Read back supplies, money, units, moves, selection and links before/after. Establish whether simply confirming triggers the rebalance, and whether timing is at arrow, disband, or OK. Do not infer no change from absence of user edits. Use private copies and keep original artifacts private; provide EXE identity/code sites/runtime provenance, a small control matrix, scalar conclusions and remaining limits. No original launch is authorized in this build session, and no remake change is requested here.

Separate from [build1486](https://github.com/diegoami/imperial_conquest_2/issues/1486) paid signed supply staging and [1488](https://github.com/diegoami/imperial_conquest_2/issues/1488) per-unit partial transfer admission.
